                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Let Me Be Honest With You", body: "I didn't grow up religious. I didn't read the Bible. I didn't meditate. I didn't do yoga. I was an engineer. I solved problems with logic, architecture, and code. If you couldn't prove it, measure it, or debug it, I wasn't interested.\n\nSo when someone first mentioned \"shadow work\" to me, I literally said: \"What?\"\n\nShadow? Like... my physical shadow? A dark side? Star Wars stuff? What does this have to do with my actual life?\n\nAnd then someone explained it in a way that hit different. They said:\n\n\"Your mind is a codebase. You've been writing code since childhood — every experience, every trauma, every belief your parents handed you, every rule school drilled into you. Most of that code is running in the background right now. You've never reviewed it. You've never refactored it. And it's causing bugs in production.\"\n\nThat's when it clicked.\n\nI'm a senior iOS engineer. I've built apps with hundreds of thousands of lines of code. I know what happens when legacy code runs unchecked. I know what happens when you inherit a codebase nobody documented. I know what technical debt does to a system over time.\n\nShadow work is just... applying those same skills to yourself."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Why Engineers Need This Most", body: "Here's the irony. Engineers are trained to debug EXTERNAL systems all day — find the root cause, trace the stack, fix the logic error, ship the patch. We're world-class at it.\n\nBut we never turn those skills inward.\n\nInstead, we:\n• Overwork instead of feeling (\"I'll just code until midnight, that'll fix the anxiety\")\n• Intellectualize instead of processing (\"I understand WHY I'm angry\" ≠ actually processing anger)\n• Optimize everything external while our internal system crashes silently\n• Wonder why we keep hitting the same walls — same relationship patterns, same burnout cycles, same impostor syndrome episodes\n\nAnd then someone says \"have you tried shadow work?\" and we roll our eyes because it sounds like crystal-waving nonsense.\n\nBut it's not. It's the most rigorous debugging protocol you'll ever run. And unlike your production app, this system has been accumulating technical debt for 20, 30, 40 years with ZERO code review.\n\nLet me show you the architecture."),
