                subtitle: "Architecture, memory leaks, and legacy code",
                emoji: "🏗️",
                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Architecture", body: "Let's map it.\n\nCONSCIOUS MIND = Your IDE\nThe code you can see. Your active thoughts, decisions, current focus. This is maybe 5-10% of total processing. You think this is \"you.\" It's the tip.\n\nSUBCONSCIOUS = Background Processes\nHabits, emotional reactions, muscle memory, learned behaviors. Runs without your input. You set these up years ago and forgot. Like cron jobs from 2009 that are still executing.\n\nSHADOW = Hidden/Suppressed Code\nThis is the code that was deliberately pushed out of the main branch. Not deleted — HIDDEN. Moved to a private repo you don't have access to. Except it's still executing. Still allocating memory. Still affecting output. You just can't see it in your IDE.\n\nCOLLECTIVE UNCONSCIOUS = The Operating System\nJung's deepest layer. Think of it as the OS your individual app runs on — universal human patterns (archetypes) that every human shares. Status-seeking, belonging needs, threat detection, hero/villain narratives. You didn't write this code. Evolution did. It ships with every human.\n\nNow here's the problem: your Shadow is full of code that was written by a 5-year-old, a 12-year-old, a scared teenager — versions of you that didn't have your current skills. But that code is still in production. Running your emotional responses. Shaping your relationships. Making decisions you think are rational but are actually just... legacy code firing."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Common Bugs in the Engineer's Shadow", body: "Let me get specific because I've lived these:\n\nBUG #1 — THE EMOTION SUPPRESSION MEMORY LEAK\nif emotion.detected() {\n    emotion.suppress() // \"Not now, I'm working\"\n    intellectualize(emotion) // \"I understand why I feel this way\"\n    // NOTE: emotion not actually deallocated\n    // Still consuming memory\n    // Will cause crash at 3am or during next argument\n}\n\nYou think you've handled the emotion because you UNDERSTOOD it. Understanding is not processing. It's like reading the error log without fixing the bug. The emotion stays in memory, leaking resources until it forces a crash — an outburst, a breakdown, insomnia, physical symptoms.\n\nBUG #2 — THE PROJECTION REDIRECT\nfunc evaluateCoworker(_ person: Person) -> Assessment {\n    // BUG: checking own shadow traits, not actual person\n    if self.shadow.contains(.anger) {\n        return .hostile // \"They're always so aggressive\"\n    }\n    // The anger is yours. You projected it.\n}\n\nEvery time someone \"triggers\" you disproportionately — that coworker who annoys you way more than they should, that personality type you can't stand — you're not seeing them clearly. You're seeing your own disowned trait reflected back at you. The brain literally can't tell the difference. Same neural pathways fire.\n\nBUG #3 — THE INFINITE LOOP (\"Why Does This Keep Happening?\")\nwhile true {\n    enterRelationship(type: .familiar)\n    repeatConflictPattern()\n    breakUp(reason: \"They were the problem\")\n    // No exit condition because pattern is unconscious\n    // Will loop until shadow code is reviewed\n}\n\nSame type of partner. Same argument at month 3. Same burnout cycle at every job. Same distance from your family. You change the inputs (new person, new company, new city) but the output is identical because the PROCESSING CODE hasn't changed.\n\nBUG #4 — THE FALSE OPTIMIZATION\nfunc optimizeLife() {\n    work.hours += 20 // \"I'll just work harder\"\n    gym.sessions += 3 // \"I'll optimize my body\"\n    productivity.apps += 5 // \"I need a better system\"\n    // Actual issue: unprocessed grief from 2019\n    // None of this addresses the root cause\n}\n\nEngineers love to optimize. But optimizing the wrong thing is worse than doing nothing. When the real issue is emotional — grief, fear, shame, unprocessed trauma — no amount of habit-tracking or productivity hacking will fix it. You're polishing the UI while the database is corrupted."),
