                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Git History You Never Read", body: "Every piece of shadow code has a commit history. You just never looked at it. Let me show you the major commit sources.\n\nCOMMIT SOURCE 1 — Family (Ages 0-7)\nThis is your initial codebase. You didn't write it — it was written FOR you.\n\n• Dad never showed emotion → commit: suppress_vulnerability.swift\n• Mom's love was conditional on achievement → commit: self_worth_equals_performance.swift\n• Parents fought about money → commit: money_equals_danger.swift\n• Sibling got attention for being loud → commit: suppress_needs_be_invisible.swift\n\nThese commits happened before you could think critically. They went straight into production with no code review. And they're STILL running.\n\nCOMMIT SOURCE 2 — School (Ages 5-18)\n• \"Sit down and be quiet\" → commit: suppress_energy_creativity.swift\n• Bullied for being different → commit: conform_to_survive.swift\n• Praised only for grades → commit: value_equals_output.swift\n• Punished for questioning authority → commit: obey_dont_think.swift\n\n13 years of daily commits to your shadow repo. Every day, 8 hours a day, the system was programmed.\n\nCOMMIT SOURCE 3 — Culture (Always Running)\n• \"Real men don't cry\" → commit: masculinity_requires_numbness.swift\n• \"Success means sacrifice\" → commit: rest_is_weakness.swift\n• \"Don't air dirty laundry\" → commit: hide_problems.swift\n• \"Be grateful, others have it worse\" → commit: invalidate_own_pain.swift\n\nCOMMIT SOURCE 4 — Trauma (Timestamps Vary)\nThe big ones. The commits that got pushed directly to main with no PR, no review, no tests.\n\n• Betrayal → commit: trust_no_one.swift\n• Abandonment → commit: never_depend_on_anyone.swift\n• Humiliation → commit: never_be_vulnerable_again.swift\n• Loss → commit: dont_love_too_deeply.swift\n\nTrauma commits have the highest priority in the runtime. They override everything else. Your logical brain says \"this person is safe\" but the trauma commit fires first: DENIED. The amygdala doesn't care about your rational analysis. It has root access."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Why Understanding + Knowing ≠ Fixed", body: "Here's where engineers get stuck. We think understanding the architecture IS the fix.\n\nIt's not.\n\nKnowing that suppress_vulnerability.swift exists in your codebase doesn't stop it from executing. You can read the source code all day. You can explain it to your therapist. You can draw a perfect diagram of your childhood dynamics.\n\nThe code is still running.\n\nThis is the critical distinction that took me forever to get:\n\nINTELLECTUAL UNDERSTANDING = Reading the error log\nEMOTIONAL PROCESSING = Actually fixing the bug\n\nYou have to FEEL the code execute, catch it in real-time, and consciously choose a different path. That's the refactor. That's the actual work.\n\nYou can't think your way out of a feeling. You can't architect your way out of grief. You can't optimize your way out of shame.\n\nYou have to FEEL it. Process it. Let it complete its execution cycle. Then — and only then — can you write the replacement code.\n\nFor an engineer, this is the hardest lesson. Our superpower (logic, analysis, systems thinking) is also our biggest shadow trap. We use it to AVOID the feeling while convincing ourselves we're \"working on it.\"\n\nReading about swimming is not swimming. Analyzing your emotions is not feeling them."),
